<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanegashima</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tanegashima is an island south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagoshima-prefecture">Kagoshima Prefecture</a>. Portuguese traders shipwrecked there in 1543 brought the first European firearms to Japan, and the local lord had them copied, so that early Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matchlock">matchlocks</a> were called tanegashima. The island is now home to Japan's main space launch centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tanegashima.jpg" alt="Tanegashima" width="320" height="557" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Image Science and Analysis Laboratory, NASA - Johnson Space Center. &quot;The Gateway to Astronaut Photography of Earth. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanegashima_ISS048.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Portuguese traders who landed on <b>Tanegashima</b> in 1543 introduced the arquebus to Japan, where gunsmiths quickly copied it and changed Sengoku-era warfare.</blockquote><a href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>In Japan, where Portuguese traders brought the arquebus to the island of <b>Tanegashima</b> in 1543, local smiths were soon making guns in large numbers.</blockquote><a href="/essays/the-military-revolution">The Military Revolution</a></li><li><blockquote>Portuguese guns reached the Shimazu vassals on <b>Tanegashima</b> in 1543, and Francis Xavier landed at Kagoshima in 1549.</blockquote><a href="/state/shimazu-clan-domain">Shimazu clan domain</a></li></ul></section>
